  "scenarios": [
    "cancel-while-waiting: the client leaves while its request waits for a place; the request never reaches the engine and its place in the line is freed.",
    "cancel-during-prompt: the client leaves while the engine reads a long prompt and nothing has been sent; the gateway notices without a failed send, aborts the engine request, and frees the quota once that request has ended.",
    "cancel-during-stream: the client leaves mid-stream; the engine request is aborted, and the quota is freed only after the gateway's engine request has ended. The test measures how long the fake engine went on after the client left.",
    "queue-full: with the caps of the service block, the request past Active plus Waiting gets 429 queue_full and never reaches the engine; the same for one outside key past its own caps.",
    "readers-reserved: with the shared places full and outside and internal requests waiting, a reader starts at once while reader places are free.",
    "shared-order: with the shared places full, the first freed shared place goes to a waiting agent or internal request before an outside request that waited longer; within a class, arrival order.",
    "count-quota: a third count of one outside key at once gets 429 queue_full; with all count places taken, a reader's count waits for a place instead of being refused.",
    "tokenize-hangs: the engine does not answer a count; at the class wall time the gateway answers 504 timeout, and the count place is free again.",
    "wall-time: a request past its wall time is cancelled with timeout, as 504 before the stream or as an error event after it.",
    "drain-races-request: requests of each class accepted before a drain, and requests arriving during it. Waiting ones of every class get 503 draining. An active outside one is cancelled at once: 503 draining if its stream has not started (the engine is still reading its prompt), else the error event draining. Our active ones finish, or at the drain deadline end the same two ways. A request arriving after the drain began gets 503 with the current status, draining or drained. None is left without an answer.",
    "drain-cancels-outside: an active outside stream is cancelled at the drain and ends without [DONE]; our active requests finish; after the drain deadline they are cancelled too, and the state turns drained.",
    "late-open-after-restart: an open carrying the previous boot_id after a restart is refused with stale_boot.",
    "error-bodies-are-safe: no error answer and no log row contains any part of the request body, on every error path."
  ]
}
